.\" Man page for woodwardcheck
.\" Contact: https://github.com/woodwardcheck/woodwardcheck
.TH WOODWARDCHECK 1 "January 2024" "woodwardcheck 1.0.0" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
woodwardcheck \- Security Audit Tool for Woodward EasyGen Controllers

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B woodwardcheck
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fITARGET\fR
.br
.B woodwardcheck
\-\-list\-checks
.br
.B woodwardcheck
\-\-list\-profiles
.br
.B woodwardcheck
\-\-help

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B woodwardcheck
is a comprehensive security auditing tool designed for Woodward EasyGen
generator controllers, with specific focus on the 3500XT model. It performs
security checks, vulnerability assessments, and configuration audits to
ensure industrial control systems meet security best practices and
compliance requirements such as IEC 62443.

.SH OPTIONS

.SS "Target Options"
.TP
.I TARGET
IP address or hostname of the target device to audit.

.SS "Connection Options"
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port " " \fIPORT\fR
Target port number. Default: 502 (Modbus TCP).

.TP
.BR \-\-protocol " " \fIPROTOCOL\fR
Communication protocol to use. Options: modbus\-tcp, http, https, snmp, vnc, telnet, ssh.
Default: modbus\-tcp.

.TP
.BR \-\-timeout " " \fISECONDS\fR
Connection timeout in seconds. Default: 30.

.SS "Protocol Port Options"
.TP
.BR \-\-modbus\-port " " \fIPORT\fR
Modbus TCP port. Default: 502.

.TP
.BR \-\-http\-port " " \fIPORT\fR
HTTP port. Default: 80.

.TP
.BR \-\-https\-port " " \fIPORT\fR
HTTPS port. Default: 443.

.TP
.BR \-\-snmp\-port " " \fIPORT\fR
SNMP port. Default: 161.

.TP
.BR \-\-vnc\-port " " \fIPORT\fR
VNC port. Default: 5900.

.TP
.BR \-\-telnet\-port " " \fIPORT\fR
Telnet port. Default: 23.

.TP
.BR \-\-ssh\-port " " \fIPORT\fR
SSH port. Default: 22.

.SS "Authentication Options"
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-username " " \fIUSERNAME\fR
Username for device authentication.

.TP
.BR \-P ", " \-\-password " " \fIPASSWORD\fR
Password for device authentication.

.TP
.BR \-\-password\-file " " \fIFILE\fR
Read password from file (more secure than command line).

.SS "Scan Options"
.TP
.BR \-\-profile " " \fIPROFILE\fR
Use a predefined scan profile. Available profiles:
.RS
.TP
.B quick\-scan
Fast scan with essential checks only.
.TP
.B full\-audit
Comprehensive security audit of all checks.
.TP
.B compliance\-62443
IEC 62443 compliance-focused audit.
.TP
.B network\-only
Network security checks only.
.RE

.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-category " " \fICATEGORIES\fR
Comma-separated list of check categories to run.
Available categories: auth, net, cfg, fw, proto, crypto.

.TP
.BR \-\-checks " " \fICHECK_IDS\fR
Comma-separated list of specific check IDs to run.
Example: AUTH\-001,NET\-001,CFG\-001

.TP
.BR \-\-exclude " " \fICHECK_IDS\fR
Comma-separated list of check IDs to exclude.

.TP
.BR \-\-min\-severity " " \fILEVEL\fR
Minimum severity level to report. Options: critical, high, medium, low, info.

.TP
.BR \-\-safe\-mode
Only run safe, read-only checks (default: enabled).

.TP
.BR \-\-no\-safe\-mode
Disable safe mode. Allows potentially disruptive checks.
Use with caution on production systems.

.SS "Output Options"
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-format " " \fIFORMAT\fR
Output report format. Options: text, html, json, markdown, rtf.
Default: text.

.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIFILE\fR
Write report to file. If not specified, output goes to stdout.

.TP
.BR \-\-no\-evidence
Exclude detailed evidence from the report.

.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable verbose output with more detailed information.

.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Quiet mode with minimal output.

.TP
.BR \-\-no\-color
Disable colored terminal output.

.SS "Configuration Options"
.TP
.BR \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
Path to YAML configuration file.

.TP
.BR \-\-log\-file " " \fIFILE\fR
Path to log file for detailed logging.

.TP
.BR \-\-log\-level " " \fILEVEL\fR
Log verbosity level. Options: debug, info, warning, error.
Default: info.

.SS "Information Options"
.TP
.B \-\-list\-checks
List all available security checks and exit.

.TP
.B \-\-list\-profiles
List available scan profiles and exit.

.TP
.B \-\-list\-categories
List check categories and exit.

.TP
.B \-\-version
Display version information and exit.

.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display help message and exit.

.SH CHECK CATEGORIES

.TP
.B AUTH
Authentication & Access Control checks including default credentials,
password policies, and session management.

.TP
.B NET
Network Security checks including port scanning, service detection,
network segmentation assessment, VNC security audit (NET-007),
Telnet security audit (NET-008), and SSH security audit (NET-009).

.TP
.B CFG
Configuration Security checks including logging, NTP, backup
configuration, and factory defaults detection.

.TP
.B FW
Firmware & Updates checks including version analysis and
known CVE detection.

.TP
.B PROTO
Communication Protocol checks including Modbus, HTTP/HTTPS,
and SNMP security.

.TP
.B CRYPTO
Cryptographic Controls checks including encryption configuration
and certificate validation.

.SH SEVERITY LEVELS

.TP
.B CRITICAL
Immediate risk requiring urgent attention. Examples: default credentials,
no authentication required, critical CVEs.

.TP
.B HIGH
Significant security risk. Examples: outdated firmware, insecure protocols,
weak encryption.

.TP
.B MEDIUM
Moderate risk that should be addressed. Examples: logging disabled,
excessive session timeout.

.TP
.B LOW
Minor issues with limited impact. Examples: NTP not configured,
informational findings.

.TP
.B INFO
Informational findings that may warrant review.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success. No failed security checks.
.TP
.B 1
Failed checks found with medium or low severity.
.TP
.B 2
Critical or high severity findings detected.

.SH EXAMPLES

.TP
Run a basic audit:
.B woodwardcheck 192.168.1.100

.TP
Quick scan with HTML report:
.B woodwardcheck 192.168.1.100 \-\-profile quick\-scan \-f html \-o report.html

.TP
Run only authentication checks:
.B woodwardcheck 192.168.1.100 \-\-category auth

.TP
Run specific checks with verbose output:
.B woodwardcheck 192.168.1.100 \-\-checks AUTH\-001,NET\-001 \-v

.TP
Full audit with JSON output for automation:
.B woodwardcheck 192.168.1.100 \-\-profile full\-audit \-f json \-o audit.json

.TP
Only report high severity and above:
.B woodwardcheck 192.168.1.100 \-\-min\-severity high

.TP
Use configuration file:
.B woodwardcheck \-\-config /etc/woodwardcheck/config.yaml

.TP
List all available checks:
.B woodwardcheck \-\-list\-checks

.TP
Run VNC and Telnet security audit with custom ports:
.B woodwardcheck 192.168.1.100 \-\-vnc\-port 5901 \-\-telnet\-port 2323

.TP
Run SSH security audit on non-standard port:
.B woodwardcheck 192.168.1.100 \-\-ssh\-port 2222 \-\-checks NET\-009

.SH CONFIGURATION FILE
The configuration file uses YAML format. Example:

.nf
target:
  host: 192.168.1.100
  port: 502
  protocol: modbus\-tcp
  timeout: 30

scan:
  categories:
    \- auth
    \- net
    \- cfg
  min_severity: medium
  safe_mode: true

output:
  format: html
  path: ./reports/
  include_evidence: true

logging:
  level: INFO
  file: ./woodwardcheck.log
.fi

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WOODWARDCHECK_CONFIG
Path to default configuration file.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/woodwardcheck/config.yaml
System-wide configuration file.

.TP
.I ~/.config/woodwardcheck/config.yaml
User configuration file.

.TP
.I ./woodwardcheck.yaml
Local directory configuration file.

.SH SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
.B woodwardcheck
is designed for authorized security testing only. Always ensure
you have proper authorization before scanning any systems.

Safe mode (enabled by default) ensures only read-only checks are
performed, preventing disruption to production systems. Disable
safe mode with caution.

The tool does not store credentials. Use \-\-password\-file for
secure password handling instead of command-line arguments.

.SH COMPLIANCE
The tool maps findings to IEC 62443 requirements where applicable,
supporting compliance audits for industrial control systems.

